! large-union-variant: union variant `huge_array` is 2048 bytes, which is significantly larger than the average of other variants (2 bytes)
  @ test.idl:7:18

 2 │ union MyUnion switch (octet) {
 3 │     case 1: char var1;
   │                  ˆˆˆˆ 1 bytes
 4 │     case 2: short var2;
   │                   ˆˆˆˆ 2 bytes
 5 │     case 3: long var3;
   │                  ˆˆˆˆ 4 bytes
 6 │     case 4: char var4;
   │                  ˆˆˆˆ 1 bytes
 7 │     case 5: char huge_array[2048];  // Much larger than all others
   │                  ˆˆˆˆˆˆˆˆˆˆ large variant (2048 bytes)
 8 │ };

  * consider annotating large variants with `@shared` to heap allocate them
